## Proposed full corrected `docs/testing.md`

```markdown
# Testing

## Setup

- **Framework:** Vitest 4.x
- **Unit / component tests:** `vitest.test.config.ts` at the repo root
- **Integration tests:** `vitest.integration.config.ts` at the repo root
- **AI evaluation tests:** `vitest.eval.config.ts` at the repo root
- No E2E or Playwright setup currently exists.

## Test File Locations

Tests are co-located with the source they cover, anywhere under `src/` (apps and shared
packages alike). The file extension determines which suite it belongs to:

| Kind             | Pattern                              | Config / command                                        |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Unit / component | `*.test.ts`, `*.test.tsx`            | `vitest.test.config.ts` · `yarn root:test`              |
| Integration      | `*.integration.test.ts` / `.tsx`     | `vitest.integration.config.ts` · `yarn root:test:integration` |
| AI evaluation    | `*.eval.ts` / `.tsx`                 | `vitest.eval.config.ts` · `yarn root:eval`              |

The unit config excludes `*.integration.test.*`, so integration tests run only via the
integration command.

## Running Tests

```bash
# Run all unit tests
yarn root:test

# Run with a filter (file name or test name pattern)
yarn root:test <filter>

# Watch mode
yarn root:test --watch

# Run integration tests
yarn root:test:integration

# Run AI evaluation tests
yarn root:eval
```

## Writing Tests

```typescript
import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";

describe("MyModule", () => {
    it("should handle the happy path", () => {
        const result = myFunction("input");
        expect(result).toBe("expected");
    });
});
```

## Test Data Management

Development and test environments never use production data. All non-production data is
synthetic.

- **Local development** runs against local Docker Postgres/Redis (see the Development Guide).
  The database is populated by the seed script
  (`src/apps/server/tenant-api/src/database/seed.ts`), which uses the open-source
  `drizzle-seed` library to generate deterministic, fictional records (e.g. a single
  "Dev Tenant"). No production data is ever exported or imported.
- **Automated tests** build their own in-test fixtures. AI evaluation tests use checked-in
  synthetic fixtures (`src/apps/server/worker/src/extractInsightWorker/exhaustiveEvalFixtures`).
  No production data is referenced.
- **Environment separation** — `development` and `production` are provisioned as separate
  Terraform stacks (`terraform/environments/app-development` vs `app-production`) with
  separate resource groups, storage accounts, databases, and database-access groups
  (`sg_normain_dev_db_accessor` vs `sg_normain_prod_db_accessor`). No database server is
  shared between environments, so production data cannot flow into dev/test.
```

